From 35472b6a498dfc0fe96373864f19328a8ef806c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:04:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/sensor: ISL29125 RGB light sensor, the Color 2 Click

isl29125 at I2C 0x44: fifteen registers behind an auto-incrementing
pointer, green/red/blue conversions in the order the mode picks on the
virtual clock (101 ms each at 16 bits, 1/16 of that at 12), 375 or 10000
lux full scale, the threshold interrupt with its persistence and the
conversion-done interrupt on the open-drain INT, both cleared by reading
STATUS, the brownout flag and the 0x46 reset. The light it sees is a
colour and a brightness ("red", "green", "blue", "lux"); each channel
counts the linearised component plus the one-count dark level. qtest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
